{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas","id":1485559,"title":"Promise of 1528, event and fun ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-01T16:10:09-07:00","id":1485559,"title":"Promise of 1528, event and fun ideas?","content":"So, how you people think occurred the Promise between the Camarilla and Giovanni Clan? And what repercussions did it had immediately?<br /> <br /> I'm running a Giovanni Chronicles game, and at the same time a Transylvania Chronicles one parallel to it (with the same players, different PCs). And I'm currently at the Convention of Thorns with both coteries and games intertwined. But, while Transylvania goes with smaller jumps to the next chapters, Giovanni Chron. goes hooping from 1444 to 1666, which is way too much, so the players would have to make way too much choices for characters that played a couple of fast chapters and now the Convention of Thorns. So I wanted to have some sessions, no more than 3, around the Promise of 1528, and was wondering what kind of game could there be. <br /> <br /> The final meeting or signing of the Promise may have happened in Rome, Florence, Milan, Venice or some place else maybe in the Holy Roman Empire. Probably some Justicar and archons were present (if not most Justicars, like they were in Transylvania to stop the Conspiracy of Isaac bur failed), and I imagine Augustus, Claudius, Ambrogino and maybe even some other traitor Cappadocian turned-Giovanni by baptism of the blood of their kin, or simply other Giovannis. Besides staying out of each others business - like a mutual pact of non-aggression and non-interference, baring Masquerade breaches I suppose - what else went immediately into effect?<br /> <br /> <br /> What kind of stories could be made about it? Prior, during or right after the signing of the Promise? I don't think there is much space for interference of the PCs into the big points of the Promise but there could be some exceptions, some minor rulings, especially in exchange for something. <br /> In this particular game, the Children of Isaac are even if shadily and loosely associated with the Camarilla, and definitely aren't friends of the Giovanni, who they ruined the ritual-diablerie and cut Claudius arm off right after his diablerie of Japheth (although it wasn't for any love of the Cappadocians). But one of the characters is actually an Archon now, so he is very likely to be there in the Promise locale, some way or another. <br /> <br /> General ideas about the Promise's event, possible laws and rules listed in it, and the effects of it, would be a very nice for the topic as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T21:00:11-07:00","id":1485594,"title":"","content":"My take on the Promise is that it is based around the assumption that they're dealing with a Antediluvian. The Inner Council knows their claims of the Antediluvians not existing is bullshit and they believe that Augustus Giovanni devoured Cappadocius. So, they're dealing with something that could become a new Tremere Clan.<br /> <br /> The Promise seems like it was probably a non-interference pact with the Giovanni as well as their business.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will not attempt to seize cities or praxis.<br /> <br /> * Giovanni might be welcome at Elysium and in Camarilla cities but can't take any positions in court (this might be more flexible)<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will not join or support the Sabbat or Anarchs that haven't folded into the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will not attempt to join the Camarilla, which is probably because the Camarilla is afraid that they will have too much power with a recently alive Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> * Giovanni who announce themselves to a Prince will be subject to the Traditions and its protections like any other vampire.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will be allowed ONE city where they rule (Venice) and can operate from.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni are allowed to gather financial power and political power among mortals to their hearts content.<br /> <br /> * Possibly the Giovanni are restricted in their numbers of Embraces per year (which works out for the Giovanni since their numbers of deaths are far less staying out of the Jyhad)<br /> <br /> * The Cappadocians will receive no aid from the Camarilla and can be slaughtered by the Giovanni at will. This means that Giovanni won't be persecuted for their diablerie or murder of the Cappadocians in any domain they do it.<br /> <br /> * The Camarilla may report any Cappadocians they find to the Giovanni (they won't protect them or actively help in the hunt, though). Being the Camarilla, I expect they'd make it clear that such information would have to be paid for and the &quot;default&quot; state is they'll just turn a blind eye to the vampirecide.<br /> <br /> You might even retcon the weirdest element of the Giovanni as being part of the Promise.<br /> <br /> &quot;We will only Embrace members of our family&quot; with the Giovanni getting around that by keeping an extensive mortal breeding stock and marrying other families.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-02-2022, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T23:22:32-07:00","id":1485603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485594#post1485594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the Promise is that it is based around the assumption that they're dealing with a Antediluvian. The Inner Council knows their claims of the Antediluvians not existing is bullshit and they believe that Augustus Giovanni devoured Cappadocius. So, they're dealing with something that could become a new Tremere Clan.<br /> <br /> The Promise seems like it was probably a non-interference pact with the Giovanni as well as their business.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will not attempt to seize cities or praxis.<br /> <br /> * Giovanni might be welcome at Elysium and in Camarilla cities but can't take any positions in court (this might be more flexible)<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will not join or support the Sabbat or Anarchs that haven't folded into the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will not attempt to join the Camarilla, which is probably because the Camarilla is afraid that they will have too much power with a recently alive Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> * Giovanni who announce themselves to a Prince will be subject to the Traditions and its protections like any other vampire.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will be allowed ONE city where they rule (Venice) and can operate from.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni are allowed to gather financial power and political power among mortals to their hearts content.<br /> <br /> * Possibly the Giovanni are restricted in their numbers of Embraces per year (which works out for the Giovanni since their numbers of deaths are far less staying out of the Jyhad)<br /> <br /> * The Cappadocians will receive no aid from the Camarilla and can be slaughtered by the Giovanni at will. This means that Giovanni won't be persecuted for their diablerie or murder of the Cappadocians in any domain they do it.<br /> <br /> * The Camarilla may report any Cappadocians they find to the Giovanni (they won't protect them or actively help in the hunt, though). Being the Camarilla, I expect they'd make it clear that such information would have to be paid for and the &quot;default&quot; state is they'll just turn a blind eye to the vampirecide.<br /> <br /> You might even retcon the weirdest element of the Giovanni as being part of the Promise.<br /> <br /> &quot;We will only Embrace members of our family&quot; with the Giovanni getting around that by keeping an extensive mortal breeding stock and marrying other families.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very good very good.<br /> I agree that close to all these points is certainly involved. If not by letter by spoken words at the Promise, which is another layer of legislation loopholes and switches; all of which are liable to only be enforced if the witnesses there give two pennies to do so.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Cappadocians not getting support is a big part of it, which isn't too much stated usually.<br /> The Founders saw Cappadocius and Japheth getting diablerized firsthand. So certainly they knew the kind of power they were dealing with. Although they may not have known the Amaranth wasn't complete.<br /> <br /> Even though I can se happening, in some way I believe Camarilla had defined that Cappadocians can't join Camarilla. But some pretty good dealing had to be done by the Giovanni. Cuz yeah, war between sect and clan would be shit for the Camarilla, but they weren't that far off from the Convention where the Anarchs were mostly brought to the table (not the other way around). So I think Giovannis had to give a lot of goodies, not only to ascertain the peace (who couldn't have been better for the Cam than it was for the Gios), but get all Cappadocians for themselves. In almost one century (more like two) these Italians necromancers managed to hunt all Cappadocians down, in the middle of the Anarch Revolt and later Sabbat and Camarilla war. I like to think Giovannis gave something, especially cuz in 1444 they started the usurpation, but it got to take a while to hunt down most Cappadocians (even if they ain't full of political protection, they are Auspicious-powered and very hermit-like; lets not bring the Lamiae protection into it), so they were way too much exposed and spread. That is taking into account that they probably had the entire usurpation set in most of the continent by then, but hardly would have the same numbers of the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> I like to wonder if Giovannis had to sworn to keep Sabbat out of their own territories, to respect strict rules (like some of those CTPhipps exposed), inform Camarilla of some things and keep a hard-ruled Masquerade, that besides a massive cash settlement I imagine (which isn't that amazing for vampires to give or receive, but yet, something). Maybe even now there is Promise Gold lying around in some Elders coffers. <br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I see the Camarilla as time goes on, either forgetting the Giovanni in a way or having a symbiotic and beneficial relationship with them (their services are, after all, unique, well-executed and professional as merchant family might as well do). Or maybe they noticed too late the Necromancers grew too wide, and even found loopholes in any rulings of Embrace limit by founding these cadet branches or sub-houses around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T23:30:49-07:00","id":1485604,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni had technically murdered their Antedeluvian, so they could very easily have thrown their lot in with the Sabbat. That means they likely had a very strong negotiating position when bargaining with the Cammies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T04:48:08-07:00","id":1485616,"title":"","content":"I think any kind of far-reaching promise is... silly, given the localized nature of vampires. Making rules for &quot;all the Camarilla&quot; just doesn't work when the Princes of Jakarta, Vienna, Moscow, Austin and Sau Paulo all have extremely different ideas on how they want their city run and are only united insofar that they really, really, really don't want foreigners dictating broad policies beyond the fucking obvious (protect masquerade, don't shelter red listers) and, much like the European union can't force the Hungarian government to at least pretend to govern decently, the Camarilla can't tell it's princes &quot;Hey guys we're kicking out half our populatation and the Brujah are bad, please destabilize your city&quot; <br /> <br /> So too it's unrealistic to do anything like that with the Giovanni. &quot;don't get involved with the Jyhad&quot; is a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T08:17:24-07:00","id":1485624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485604#post1485604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni had technically murdered their Antedeluvian, so they could very easily have thrown their lot in with the Sabbat. That means they likely had a very strong negotiating position when bargaining with the Cammies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, the Camarilla Inner Council would also know that the Giovanni don't want anything to do with the Sabbat's forever war so it's less of a hand than they think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485616#post1485616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any kind of far-reaching promise is... silly, given the localized nature of vampires. Making rules for &quot;all the Camarilla&quot; just doesn't work when the Princes of Jakarta, Vienna, Moscow, Austin and Sau Paulo all have extremely different ideas on how they want their city run and are only united insofar that they really, really, really don't want foreigners dictating broad policies beyond the fucking obvious (protect masquerade, don't shelter red listers) and, much like the European union can't force the Hungarian government to at least pretend to govern decently, the Camarilla can't tell it's princes &quot;Hey guys we're kicking out half our populatation and the Brujah are bad, please destabilize your city&quot;<br /> <br /> So too it's unrealistic to do anything like that with the Giovanni. &quot;don't get involved with the Jyhad&quot; is a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni are a Clan ruled from the top down, unlike most vampire Clans.<br /> <br /> And Princes acting independently is pretty much why Justicars exist. They exist to smack down any who get too independent. They don't send them after Neonates breaking the Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T12:51:31-07:00","id":1485640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485604#post1485604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni had technically murdered their Antedeluvian, so they could very easily have thrown their lot in with the Sabbat. That means they likely had a very strong negotiating position when bargaining with the Cammies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so. I think that would be their biggest trump cards, an Ante and a join Anarchs (and then Sabbat) risk, but I still don't think that presses advantage for Giovannis, for me it levels the playing field. Of which Giovannis profit more from the treaty I think, if made dry like that without nothing given or taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T13:07:03-07:00","id":1485642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485616#post1485616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any kind of far-reaching promise is... silly, given the localized nature of vampires. Making rules for &quot;all the Camarilla&quot; just doesn't work when the Princes of Jakarta, Vienna, Moscow, Austin and Sau Paulo all have extremely different ideas on how they want their city run and are only united insofar that they really, really, really don't want foreigners dictating broad policies beyond the fucking obvious (protect masquerade, don't shelter red listers) and, much like the European union can't force the Hungarian government to at least pretend to govern decently, the Camarilla can't tell it's princes &quot;Hey guys we're kicking out half our populatation and the Brujah are bad, please destabilize your city&quot;<br /> <br /> So too it's unrealistic to do anything like that with the Giovanni. &quot;don't get involved with the Jyhad&quot; is a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A promise is a promise, and it mostly is leverage and claims to be pressed in this matter I believe. Like, ok, they won't enforce in every single city, but both Cam and Gios can bring it up at situations that matter. Situations where the higher-ups will hear and might want to act upon. And since both the sect and the clan's top leaders settled this, no elder or justicar will change it or disregard it, not without consequences from the Top. So Princes and local families will always get the shaft, instead of the Promise being ignored if conflict between the two groups. That is what I think.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Kindred ruling, be it any sect or clan is much more regional and parochial. But the structure of the Camarilla is made in a way as to hammer nails that stick out the most, not every one. I also amusingly imagine Archons most of the time just going to Cities/Princedoms to say &quot;we will let this one slide, but you gotta give X to the Camarilla Justicars (or Inner Circle)&quot;. Just like a lot of Prince laws are to oppress the small and curry favors from the big.<br /> <br /> <br /> Giovannis don't seem much different. Camarilla is almost like the police, and as dull and tiring as it is to compare Giovannis to the mob, well it is like this. They work in a parallel out-of-each-others way, sometimes symbiotic, relationship. They trade contacts, info and services to each other hush-hush, but everything under wraps and sparsely. And in some cases they got to let each other slide even if they hate doing it. <br /> I just wanted to know what the Camarilla gained besides one new rising opposition that wasn't actually interested or strong in attack with the Promise. Maybe the Ventrue and Toreador had a lot of debt in the Holy Empire and in Italy and the Necromancers got to wipe it out for them? That would be silly, but who knows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T14:09:51-07:00","id":1485647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485640#post1485640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe so. I think that would be their biggest trump cards, an Ante and a join Anarchs (and then Sabbat) risk, but I still don't think that presses advantage for Giovannis, for me it levels the playing field. Of which Giovannis profit more from the treaty I think, if made dry like that without nothing given or taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big deal being:<br /> <br /> * Augustus Giovanni is now their Antediluvian and, at least for the time being, DIRECTLY RULING their Clan.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni don't want to become involved in the Sabbat's war against all the other Antediluvians. They only want to destroy the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni are a much-much softer touch than the Sabbat and less war parties than assassins.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat are actually primarily based in the Americas as they were on their last legs before they immigrated with the colonialists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T14:11:34-07:00","id":1485650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485616#post1485616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any kind of far-reaching promise is... silly, given the localized nature of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something being silly has never stopped vampires before, and they usually resort to carnage when things don't go they way they want. It's all part of the setting and the game. The Promise has also been a part of the setting for decades, and through multiple editions. So complaining about it is also moot. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T15:10:49-07:00","id":1485654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485647#post1485647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The big deal being:<br /> <br /> * Augustus Giovanni is now their Antediluvian and, at least for the time being, DIRECTLY RULING their Clan.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni don't want to become involved in the Sabbat's war against all the other Antediluvians. They only want to destroy the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni are a much-much softer touch than the Sabbat and less war parties than assassins.<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat are actually primarily based in the Americas as they were on their last legs before they immigrated with the colonialists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm... this and what CajunKhan said gave a couple of ideas.<br /> <br /> Any idea what the Giovanni might have given, in return for a little help in hunting down some Cappadocians, with the unofficial help of some Camarilla affiliates? Not much metaplot heavy here, just idea for a small chronicle game. After all, if they are going to actively ignore Cappadocian pleads (a bit like the Salubri), why not help a bit, even if only individually (and not like a sect)?<br /> Or maybe something lese, like a little raid Camarilla want to do before Giovannis get someplace, to take away from them some Cappadocians secrets before it is actually theirs to take.<br /> <br /> It would interesting especially cuz Transylvania Chronicles later deals with Maria de Assunci\u00f3n, the last known Cappadocian (which its of course BS, but prophecies are as well). So some dealings with Cappadocians even before that (by the players, not characters; cuz this game would be with the Children of Isaac). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T15:56:12-07:00","id":1485658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485654#post1485654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhm... this and what CajunKhan said gave a couple of ideas.<br /> <br /> Any idea what the Giovanni might have given, in return for a little help in hunting down some Cappadocians, with the unofficial help of some Camarilla affiliates? Not much metaplot heavy here, just idea for a small chronicle game. After all, if they are going to actively ignore Cappadocian pleads (a bit like the Salubri), why not help a bit, even if only individually (and not like a sect)?<br /> Or maybe something lese, like a little raid Camarilla want to do before Giovannis get someplace, to take away from them some Cappadocians secrets before it is actually theirs to take.<br /> <br /> It would interesting especially cuz Transylvania Chronicles later deals with Maria de Assunci\u00f3n, the last known Cappadocian (which its of course BS, but prophecies are as well). So some dealings with Cappadocians even before that (by the players, not characters; cuz this game would be with the Children of Isaac).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Giovanni have multiple things to offer:<br /> <br /> * Their neutrality in sect matters is a big bargaining chip by itself. The Camarilla actually would pay a lot to have the Giovanni agree not to rock the boat of their rulership of Europe and Northern Asia at this time. After all, the Promise amounts to being a non-aggression pact and that often gets a lot of concessions.<br /> <br /> * Financial agreements that would be notable given the early banking systems of the world are still being established. The Ventrue's transition from nobility to merchant class might be assisted by the Giovanni in this time period.<br /> <br /> * Necromantic backup. The Camarilla might be paid in being told where the locations of sleeping Ancients or Red Listers are that they can keep an eye on them. They can also receive spy information that might be of relevance to the time.<br /> <br /> * Perhaps the Giovanni have a vast amount of blackmail material on other Elders.<br /> <br /> * If you want to be humorous, the Giovanni can provide some Da Vinci-code esque relics from the Vatican or assistance against the Society of Leopold. Maybe the Giovanni use their influence to get the Vatican to disavow the Inquisition's supernatural activities.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni may also be &quot;paying&quot; in the act.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;The Camarilla is against diablerie but sanctions it with a Blood Hunt. However, we've agreed that the Giovanni won't be punished for diablerie and execution of Cappadocians. So, how about we extend that so that if we hire anyone to kill Cappadocians and diablerize them. They won't be punished? I'm fairly sure there's a lot of Neonates who would love this. It's not the Camarilla sanctioning the murder of Cappadocians, no, that would be awful. No, it's just...ignoring if something happens to them by their neonates. With fangs.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-02-2022, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T17:17:35-07:00","id":1485665,"title":"","content":"The original clan description of the Giovanni in the 1e and 2e Players Guide mentioned the Giovanni would only embrace 3 people once a generation (which I interpreted as about once every decade). There wasn't any reason given for this, but I always associated it with the deal made between the Giovanni and the Camarilla in the Promise of 1528.<br /> <br /> From the Camarilla's perspective, the Promise of 1528 was to bring the Giovanni into the &quot;Camarilla system&quot; so they were part of the new order that the Inner Circle was establishing. They were a part of the Camarilla's &quot;great society&quot; of the undead, just not an equal part. It put strong limits on the Giovanni, but kept them part of the system instead of them becoming bitter-ender Anarchs/Sabbat. It allowed the Giovanni internal autonomy that would not be subject to Justicar supervision (who got to be embraced, internal punishment/destruction, diablerie within the clan, etc.), but kept a firm thumb on them so they couldn't run wild. <br /> <br /> I always designated the &quot;Devil Kindred&quot; to be about in the same condition as Jews were in Medieval Europe - a &quot;protected&quot;, but legally inferior, class by the Camarilla's ruling authorities. They were not to be molested, but their activities were limited and proscribed. But just like Jewish moneylenders were able to provide a useful service that Christians could not do, the Devil Kindred sometimes got to take advantage of similar things. They could be useful to Camarilla Kindred by doing things they couldn't do themselves without bringing scandal or punishment down on them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, about the only time the Promise of 1528 was mentioned was in the context of the Giovanni themselves, so it was usually mocked as nothing special, and sometimes even implied it was done to protect the Camarilla from them. I know a lot of the players of Giovanni tended to be very arrogant about it and not think it really restricted the Giovanni in any way. But I never held that view and took things differently in my own chronicles.<br /> <br /> They were subject to certain restrictions like they could never enter a domain without explicit permission from a Camarilla Prince. Although once they were there, residency couldn't be easily revoked without cause. The aforementioned restriction on how many embraces they could do. That they could not hold Status or office in a Camarilla domain. That Giovanni in a domain would need to provide certain services for the Prince if requested without need of a boon. And similar things.<br /> <br /> That's how I handled it. If you there is anything here you can make use out of for your own chronicle, go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T19:07:42-07:00","id":1485670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485658#post1485658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine the Giovanni have multiple things to offer:<br /> <br /> * Their neutrality in sect matters is a big bargaining chip by itself. The Camarilla actually would pay a lot to have the Giovanni agree not to rock the boat of their rulership of Europe and Northern Asia at this time. After all, the Promise amounts to being a non-aggression pact and that often gets a lot of concessions.<br /> <br /> * Financial agreements that would be notable given the early banking systems of the world are still being established. The Ventrue's transition from nobility to merchant class might be assisted by the Giovanni in this time period.<br /> <br /> * Necromantic backup. The Camarilla might be paid in being told where the locations of sleeping Ancients or Red Listers are that they can keep an eye on them. They can also receive spy information that might be of relevance to the time.<br /> <br /> * Perhaps the Giovanni have a vast amount of blackmail material on other Elders.<br /> <br /> * If you want to be humorous, the Giovanni can provide some Da Vinci-code esque relics from the Vatican or assistance against the Society of Leopold. Maybe the Giovanni use their influence to get the Vatican to disavow the Inquisition's supernatural activities.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni may also be &quot;paying&quot; in the act.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;The Camarilla is against diablerie but sanctions it with a Blood Hunt. However, we've agreed that the Giovanni won't be punished for diablerie and execution of Cappadocians. So, how about we extend that so that if we hire anyone to kill Cappadocians and diablerize them. They won't be punished? I'm fairly sure there's a lot of Neonates who would love this. It's not the Camarilla sanctioning the murder of Cappadocians, no, that would be awful. No, it's just...ignoring if something happens to them by their neonates. With fangs.&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's funny, cuz Giovanni Chronciles Part 2 is actually about the Vatican beieng raided by Giovanni, getting things the Camarilla actually hid there from them. The Sargon Fragment especially.<br /> In a way that is somewhat a good part of the back and forth between the Clan and the sect. You are not interfering if you are getting or hiding things that aren't theirs yet.<br /> <br /> Also, these are so good options of agreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T20:33:13-07:00","id":1485675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485665#post1485665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original clan description of the Giovanni in the 1e and 2e Players Guide mentioned the Giovanni would only embrace 3 people once a generation (which I interpreted as about once every decade). There wasn't any reason given for this, but I always associated it with the deal made between the Giovanni and the Camarilla in the Promise of 1528.<br /> <br /> From the Camarilla's perspective, the Promise of 1528 was to bring the Giovanni into the &quot;Camarilla system&quot; so they were part of the new order that the Inner Circle was establishing. They were a part of the Camarilla's &quot;great society&quot; of the undead, just not an equal part. It put strong limits on the Giovanni, but kept them part of the system instead of them becoming bitter-ender Anarchs/Sabbat. It allowed the Giovanni internal autonomy that would not be subject to Justicar supervision (who got to be embraced, internal punishment/destruction, diablerie within the clan, etc.), but kept a firm thumb on them so they couldn't run wild.<br /> <br /> I always designated the &quot;Devil Kindred&quot; to be about in the same condition as Jews were in Medieval Europe - a &quot;protected&quot;, but legally inferior, class by the Camarilla's ruling authorities. They were not to be molested, but their activities were limited and proscribed. But just like Jewish moneylenders were able to provide a useful service that Christians could not do, the Devil Kindred sometimes got to take advantage of similar things. They could be useful to Camarilla Kindred by doing things they couldn't do themselves without bringing scandal or punishment down on them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, about the only time the Promise of 1528 was mentioned was in the context of the Giovanni themselves, so it was usually mocked as nothing special, and sometimes even implied it was done to protect the Camarilla from them. I know a lot of the players of Giovanni tended to be very arrogant about it and not think it really restricted the Giovanni in any way. But I never held that view and took things differently in my own chronicles.<br /> <br /> They were subject to certain restrictions like they could never enter a domain without explicit permission from a Camarilla Prince. Although once they were there, residency couldn't be easily revoked without cause. The aforementioned restriction on how many embraces they could do. That they could not hold Status or office in a Camarilla domain. That Giovanni in a domain would need to provide certain services for the Prince if requested without need of a boon. And similar things.<br /> <br /> That's how I handled it. If you there is anything here you can make use out of for your own chronicle, go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I have a tendency more for this side of things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And sometimes it is that old case of Vampire not filling in these matters, and &quot;leaving to the Storyteller&quot; a little too much. Which isn't bad, but sometimes it is a shame. Not only the Promise in this case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T16:53:38-07:00","id":1485730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485594#post1485594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Promise seems like it was probably a non-interference pact with the Giovanni as well as their business...</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to add something silly to this, like not messing with the Netflix account of members of the Inner Circle, or killing Jedi if Order 66 is given.<br /> <br /> But I think a real addition would probably involve the regular Camarilla meetings held in Venice. I can see the Camarilla holding meetings there as a show of force, but it still feel like a bad idea. In any case, the Promise probably allowed the meetings while officially requiring the Giovanni to stay out of the way and to not spy on the proceedings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T07:17:47-07:00","id":1485768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485594#post1485594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the Promise is that it is based around the assumption that they're dealing with a Antediluvian. The Inner Council knows their claims of the Antediluvians not existing is bullshit and they believe that Augustus Giovanni devoured Cappadocius. So, they're dealing with something that could become a new Tremere Clan.<br /> <br /> The Promise seems like it was probably a non-interference pact with the Giovanni as well as their business.<br /> <br /> * The Giovanni will be allowed ONE city where they rule (Venice) and can operate from.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just one city? What about the cities in which the Giovanni more or less have the most (or close to the most) influence and resources?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485616#post1485616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any kind of far-reaching promise is... silly, given the localized nature of vampires. Making rules for &quot;all the Camarilla&quot; just doesn't work when the Princes of Jakarta, Vienna, Moscow, Austin and Sau Paulo all have extremely different ideas on how they want their city run and are only united insofar that they really, really, really don't want foreigners dictating broad policies beyond the fucking obvious (protect masquerade, don't shelter red listers) and, much like the European union can't force the Hungarian government to at least pretend to govern decently, the Camarilla can't tell it's princes &quot;Hey guys we're kicking out half our populatation and the Brujah are bad, please destabilize your city&quot;<br /> <br /> So too it's unrealistic to do anything like that with the Giovanni. &quot;don't get involved with the Jyhad&quot; is a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might in the end by that the Giovanni are treated more or less the same as other Independant Clans by Camarilla Vampires - seemingly avoided, but treated seriously on many occasions, under the right circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T10:47:22-07:00","id":1485784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485768#post1485768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one city? What about the cities in which the Giovanni more or less have the most (or close to the most) influence and resources?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I would say those would be violations of the Promise but that just adds to the realism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might in the end by that the Giovanni are treated more or less the same as other Independant Clans by Camarilla Vampires - seemingly avoided, but treated seriously on many occasions, under the right circumstances. </div> </div> </div>I feel like the Giovanni need to have a deeper deal because, well, the Camarilla ignores the genocide of a Clan that wants to join them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T13:43:51-07:00","id":1485797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485784#post1485784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I would say those would be violations of the Promise but that just adds to the realism.I mean, I would say those would be violations of the Promise but that just adds to the realism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be, because there's a difference between being the biggest game in town and trying to be the actual <i>de facto </i>boss.<br /> <br /> Venice is the Giovanni turf <i>par excellence</i>. They're not the only clan, but anyone there have to pay them tribute and respect, they're the ones running the show. You get there, you have to learn Giovanni rules, meet Giovanni officials, obey Giovanni orders, and if it comes to it, the Giovanni are the ones calling a Blood Hunt on you or whatever.<br /> <br /> As far as we know, this isn't the case anywhere else even when they have the greatest influence. Giovanni may be the most influential, but they'll keep most to themselves and deal with others just as business. That could be a perfectly valid situation within the Promise, as long as they don't overtly take office they can be influential as is and wait for other clans to come for favors instead of making threats and laws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485559-promise-of-1528-event-and-fun-ideas?p=1485784#post1485784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Giovanni need to have a deeper deal because, well, the Camarilla ignores the genocide of a Clan that wants to join them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but it is also arguably the least politically involved clan, known for taking care of their own business and generally not affecting others all that much. The kind of group you wouldn't go out of your way to harm, but also have little reason to protect too much. The Giovanni took the initiative and contacted the Cam ahead of time to set things strait before anyone could see their personal war as a greater threat than it was.<br /> <br /> At this point they don't need to offer so much, necessarily. They're offering to stay out of the way and eat up Camarilla law without any complaint, and asking just to be left to their own devices, basically saying &quot;we don't want to be or cause trouble and we'll accept your demands for proof, no questions asked&quot;. That's a powerful offer because of how little it asks from the Camarilla in any sense, it literally just asks for inaction when action would be cumbersome anyway, and trumps most offers the Cappadocians could make at the time.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Camarilla would have its own reasons to still want the Cappadocians, even if they had to go to war for them. I generally don't like the fall of the Cappadocians. But all in all I don't think it's too hard to take the Promise at face value on its basic premises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T15:26:08-07:00","id":1485802,"title":"","content":"Well, I agree with the arguments about how leaving the Cappadocians isn't a big deal, and so it kind of is a free chip to just look away. But still, I think these were times that the Camarilla would get a lot of good PR and rep if they catched the Giovanni. The Clan's strength at the time is honestly the biggest unknown weight point in the matter for me. Because I think they were still very small compared to other Clans, and especially the Camarilla. So there needed to be some very good offers for the Camarilla to let these pseudo-Anarchs go besides their Promise to stop at that, if nothing else, than to get something out of a political bullying and threat. Which.. the Giovannis might have called off, since they already took the most important components of the Cappadocians, so they weren't an interesting addition to the Sect, and so there wasn't much for the Cam to save.<br /> <br /> Either way, I still think there is chance for many possibilities.<br /> <br /> I do think Giovanni work strongly as a guild or corporation, non-surprisingly. So as it has been said already, they don't need the throne of the city to be the boss. Hell, they might even hold entire cities at gunpoint, they just need hold the Prince hostage with some real dirt on'em and then they can hold protection rackets, monopolize influences and contacts, and be the city's kings. Of cours, subtle and less egregious (less Justicar-involving) action is preferred. But holly molly, I only imagine what an Anarch domain, that doesn't collective and actively opposes them, can be for a Giovanni, a &quot;lawless&quot; land for profit and control; depending on the level of unity, order and strength of the Anarchs of course.<br /> <br /> And I don't imagine it being too hard for a Giovanni to get a branch office in a Camarilla town under the right diplomatic basis. Or even better, be given an &quot;out-of-town&quot; domain, like a satellite city or suburbia, where he can be quickly called for services, with exclusive benefits for the Prince, and restriction to work against the throne of course. I see more of the Promise as a &quot;if you play with us, you will play by our rules, or else we don't play&quot; and &quot;we don't play with other players against one another&quot;, not simply &quot;we don't nothing&quot;. And that works for both cases.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although I don't believe there is any strong limitation like &quot;you can't rule a city of your own&quot;, there might be some restrictions or regulations that really hinders that. As such, I can really see the subsidiary families coming into play. Not only it incorporates premade and prerooted structures and power lines, but it would probably be a loophole in the Promise somewhere. Even if some parts of it might say cheekly &quot;Clan of Death&quot; instead of Giovanni, just to be a bitch of a wording.<br /> <br /> In the end, it would never be hard for the Giovanni, when a member or even entire city worth of coteries of the Clan breaks the Promise, to cut them off. Claiming they were working alone. And then, an entire city of Giovanni gets hammered by Justicars. Some VIPs might be saved hush hush back to the Clan, but Giovanni are all about being good bankers and merchants, manage assets in detail, and the well-being of the corporation in the long run above all else. Only two points in their history they gambled, and even then it was secure. The first being the Embrace of the family, and the second, the Bite of the Cappadocians. The third, and last, would be the Eternal Night, the rending of the Shroud. but.... that ain't happening <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}